// nov11b washu-chan divergence_000000: the check accepted and the build
// refused "an instance at fn(a: B<[Array<'_1>, Array<'_2>]>, ..) of a
// definition typed fn(a: B<Array<'_1>>, ..)". The constructor's payload
// is a lower bound, the call merges it with the argument's, and the
// instance's variable settles to a union of two arrays nothing tells
// apart; the definition's own bound could go to either member, so
// FnType::held_at refused the choice. Either member types the body, and
// the first now takes it.
{ type B<'p> = Abstract<'p>; let pair = |a, b: B<'q>| { let c = B([never()]); a <- c }; let x = B([]); pair(x, x) }
